# .env.example — the two-machine test rig, not DPUmesh itself.
#
# This file tells the bench harness (bench/bench.sh and its siblings) which
# machines the rig is made of and how to reach them. Copy to .env and fill in;
# the harness sources it and refuses rig operations without it.
#
# Configuring DPUmesh — the DPU process, the control-plane daemons, a meshed
# Pod — is design/CONTROL.md §5.5. On a cluster those values travel in
# manifests; here the harness assembles them from this file and its own
# defaults, as a worked example of that section.

# --- Rig access: harness-only, never a production pattern ---
DPU_HOST="jukebox@<DPU_IP>"        # ssh target for the DPU (ARM+DPA build/run)
DPU_PASS="<DPU_SUDO_PASSWORD>"     # sudo on the DPU (start/stop dpumesh_dpu)
HOST_PASS="<HOST_SUDO_PASSWORD>"   # sudo on this host (ctr image import, pinning)

# --- Rig hardware: the BlueField's PCI functions on each side ---
DPU_PCI="-p 03:00.0 -r 94:00.0"    # dpumesh_dpu command line: -p device, -r host representor
HOST_PCI="94:00.0"                 # host-side function; becomes DPUMESH_PCI_ADDR

# --- Data-plane geometry this rig runs (design/CONTROL.md §5.5.1) ---
# Operator knobs, not rig facts: on a cluster these are the DPU process's
# environment plus the webhook's --rings-per-pod. The harness forwards them to
# both ends so host and DPU agree on K.
DPUMESH_DPA_THREADS=32              # N: DPA execution units
DPUMESH_RINGS_PER_POD=8             # K: forward rings per Pod
DPUMESH_ARM_WORKERS=8               # A=L: ARM workers and RX landing stripes (lowered to a divisor of K)
DPUMESH_L7_LINKERD_WORKER=all       # Linkerd runtime placement: a worker index, or "all"

# --- Optional: the inter-node carrier (design/CONTROL.md §5.5.1) ---
# Unset means no carrier binds, which is what a single-node rig wants. Naming
# one makes every ARM worker take a listener at base+w, so both nodes of a pair
# must run the same DPUMESH_ARM_WORKERS.
# DPUMESH_PEER_TRANSPORT=rdma      # rdma | tcp
# DPUMESH_PEER_BIND=10.77.0.1      # local address to bind; an rdma device's own for rdma
# DPUMESH_PEER_PORT=47900          # base port; ARM worker w takes base+w
# DPUMESH_NODE_RDMA_ADDR=10.77.0.1:47900 # optional published-address override
# DPUMESH_NODES_FILE=/etc/dpumesh/nodes  # multi-node: operator file generated with node-record

# --- Optional ---
# DPU_PROJ="DPUmesh"               # dir name of this repo on the DPU (~/$DPU_PROJ); default DPUmesh
